      "type": "narrative-update",
      "date": "2026-05-03T08:03:30.000Z",
      "title": "IEX: Coal Exchange Review And Rising Volumes Will Support Future Upside",
      "body": "The analyst fair value estimate for Indian Energy Exchange has moved from roughly ₹270 to about ₹236. The lower target reflects updated views on revenue growth, profitability, discount rates and the P/E multiple that analysts are now willing to apply.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": "https://simplywall.st/community/narratives/in/diversified-financials/nse-iex/indian-energy-exchange-shares/pvoh05or-indias-renewable-surge-will-transform-power-trading-landscape-lj3r/updates/2-the-analyst-fair-value-estimate-for-indian-energy-exchange-h",
      "raw_subtype": "narrative-update"
    },
    {
      "id": "9d1440d9-5da9-4ef8-a34c-9d62cdaf8474",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-04-25T20:57:13.000Z",
      "title": "Final dividend increased to ₹2.00",
      "body": "Dividend of ₹2.00 is 33% higher than last year. Ex-date: 15th May 2026 Payment date: 1st January 1970 Dividend yield will be 2.8%, which is higher than the industry average of 1.3%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is covered by both earnings (56% earnings payout ratio) and cash flows (64% cash payout ratio). The dividend has increased by an average of 19% per year over the past 8 years. However, payments have been volatile during that time. EPS is expected to grow by 10% over the next 2 years, which should provide support to the dividend and adequate earnings cover.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "6935fe87-ca67-4616-bae5-9c6b0381e71a",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-04-24T12:18:05.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS in line with analyst expectations despite revenue beat",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹5.54 (up from ₹4.83 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹7.47b (up 14% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹4.93b (up 15% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 66% (in line with FY 2025). Revenue exceeded analyst estimates by 1.6%. Earnings per share (EPS) were mostly in line with analyst estimates. Revenue is expected to decline by 6.8% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, while revenues in the Capital Markets industry in India are expected to grow by 16%. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 17% per year but the company’s share price has fallen by 8% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "2e757689-fb42-4a55-ba8e-4a542de1d472",
      "type": "event",
